From 9b6cc1f01f92462d45b3b45823d51b96d9e9bb66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 02:24:39 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Know the packing of a stereoscopic 3D video: show it,
 preview it, and render it

A stereoscopic 3D video holds both views in every frame, in one of the packings of the
frame packing arrangement SEI (H.264 Table D-8, H.265 Table D.8) or of Matroska's
StereoMode (RFC 9559, 5.1.4.1.28.3). MLT's avformat producer now says which
(meta.media.stereo3d.type and meta.media.stereo3d.invert), and its consumer writes it
(stereo3d and stereo3d_invert), so Kdenlive can:

- show it in the clip properties, with the size of one view;
- let each monitor show the packed frame as it is (the default) or the left eye's view
  only, for side by side and top and bottom, row and column interleaved and
  checkerboard packings (a frame sequence has one view in each frame, and is shown as
  it is), from the Stereoscopic 3D entry of the More Options menu;
- give the project a packing, from its clips unless the project monitor's menu says
  otherwise (for a video that does not say), and pass it to the render so that the
  encoder writes the frame packing arrangement SEI and the Matroska file its
  StereoMode.

Needs the MLT change that adds those properties.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
